   "text": "Restrictions\n\n- Your Army may not take Relic Wargear.\n- You may not take Warlord Traits except for those granted by this Rite of War. Unique Characters still gain the benefit of their listed Warlord trait if selected as your Warlord. You may not purchase a second Warlord trait for any models.\n- Your Army may not include the following units:\n    - Avatar of Khaine.\n    - Coven Keyword units.\n    - Mandrakes.\n    - Drazhar.\n    - Kheradruakh 'The Decapitator'.\n    - Asdrubael Vect on Dias of Destruction.\n    - Baron Sathonyx.\n    - Duke Sliscus.\n    - Asurmen.\n    - Baharroth.\n    - Fuegan.\n    - Karandras.\n    - Maugan Ra.\n    - Irilyth.\n    - Lhykis.\n\nBenefits\n\n- Your Primary Detachment may include units from Codex: Craftworlds, Codex: Dark Eldar, Codex Supplement: Corsairs & Codex Supplement: Exodites.\n- All units in your army gain the Ynnari Keyword.\n- All Ynnari units in your army replace the Battle Focus, Unbound Arrogance, Power from Pain and Word Spirit special rules with Strength from Death (see below).\n- Any Eldar unit in your army which gains access to the Runes of Fate Psychic Discipline instead must purchase the Psychic Powers listed on the Revenant Discipline (see below).\n- Your army gains access to the Ynnari Warlord Traits (see below).\n- You gain access to the following units (see below):\n    - Yvraine, Herald of Ynnead.\n    - Visarch.\n    - Yncarne, Avatar of Ynnead.\n\nYnnari Warlord Traits\n\n- Favoured of Ynnead\n- Lord of Rebirth\n- Master of Death\n\nRevenant Discipline",
